From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dale Curtis <dalecurtis@chromium.org>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 18:54:27 -0800
Subject: [Media] Align MultiBuffer redirect handling with Blink loading stack

Align ResourceMultiBufferDataProvider and UrlIndex redirect handling
with Blink's ResourceLoader, ResourceFetcher, and network-service
redirect rules:

1. Retarget normal forward HTTP redirects onto UrlIndex (via a named
   UrlData::Key struct) while latching UrlData::ServiceWorkerMode::kSkip
   (gated on media::kDisallowMixedOpaqueMediaResponses) whenever a
   redirect hop was not fetched via a Service Worker
   (!WasFetchedViaServiceWorker()), matching
   ResourceLoader::WillFollowRedirectInternal and
   ResourceFetcher::GetCacheIdentifier. Pass SetSkipServiceWorker(true)
   on retargeted follow-up range requests so embedding Service Workers
   cannot observe post-redirect URLs, while preserving offline Service
   Worker caching for direct loads and synthetic Response.redirect()
   hops under separate UrlIndex keys.
2. Track hop-by-hop cross-origin redirects (via previous_url) and
   worst-case chain relation (via net::GetOriginRelation()) in a
   per-request RedirectState reset on Start(), enforcing consistent
   has_cross_origin_redirect state in UrlData::CanAcceptDataFrom(). When
   direct follow-up range requests to the post-redirect URL would lose
   redirect-chain relation or tainting (bounce-back chains where
   final_relation < max_origin_relation, or no-cors cross-origin
   redirects under universal/extension access), allocate an unindexed
   UrlData via NewUnindexedUrlData() that reports the post-redirect URL
   via url() while continuing to use original_request_url_ via
   request_url() on follow-up range requests.
3. Rely directly on UrlData::is_cors_cross_origin() for
   MultiBufferDataSource::WouldTaintOrigin() (removing the redundant
   single_origin_ flag and unused MediaLogProperty::kIsSingleOrigin),
   and monotonically latch Timing-Allow-Origin failures across redirect
   hops, accepted range responses, RedirectTo(), and MergeFrom().

